# Touchstone-86, soak_fault: run until failure: a pass of the soak (AD 01), then D5 of the odd bank stuck low stops it at F2 02.
# For DS1 (LO on the silk): set CONST ROLE = 1 in Touchstone.bas.
# Written by TTLSim's TouchstoneRomTests from tstrom.asm on Ida's 8086 core at 4 MHz; not edited by hand.
# Power-on at 0; the CPU leaves reset at 250 ms.
THING OledThing
0.000 B=5A
250.042 B=00
9193.713 B=01
10005.159 B=FF
10010.461 B=02
10015.780 B=10
10021.098 B=22
10026.417 B=31
10031.738 B=40
10037.056 B=50
10042.375 B=60
10047.693 B=70
10053.016 B=8F
10058.334 B=9F
10063.653 B=AF
10068.971 B=BF
10074.294 B=CD
10079.612 B=DF
10084.931 B=EF
10090.249 B=FF
10095.556 B=02
END 10596.000
